Z||000004||btoth||10-05-2001||09:42 PM||||The only *bad* things I've noticed where posted above.  Otherwise I notice no difference.  Internet Explorer itself has new "features" like auto image resizing... which just seems dumb because it takes 10 times longer to view an image (even with my DSL) so I turned it off.  I turned off the media bars and any other extra junk the IE thinks you need... so now it's just like normal.  I'm sure there were some fixes to something, just nothing that affected me.  BTW, I'm running Win 2k, so that might have something to do with me not noticing any difference... besides that stupid num lock thing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  And as far as the "spyware" that every internet app uses now, I run my AdAware program regularly and haven't found anything new.||||reg||1
