Z||000011||grinthock||10-08-2001||10:33 AM||||VERY SIMPLE ---<P>ANSWER TO QUESTION:  Why must my ACTIVE DESKTOP be enabled to show a desktop image.<P>IT DOESN'T!!  You must enable active desktop to show a JPG, or GIF image on your desktop but NOT a BMP!  BMP files are windows specific and are the native format for the desktop.  SO, convert the file into a BMP, then turn off active desktop, then select that as your wallpaper!||||reg||1
Z||000012||DJRice||10-08-2001||10:28 PM||||Yeah, because that "Set image as wallpaper" option that created a BMP from any image you right-clicked was just to darned complicated...<P>Microsoft 'improves' their products by adding overhead.  Its the equivalent of any Fortune 500 Company doubling the amount of senior manager and director level positions in an attempt to increase efficiency...It just wont happen.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> <BR>"And this one time, on the Fiero Forum..."||||reg||1
Z||000013||btoth||10-09-2001||10:21 AM||||I found out that something (IE 6.0) screwed up my registry... I had to manually go in and delete all the registry entries for IIS to get it to work again.  My FTP problem was completely unrelated and I got that fixed, but not until <I>after</I> I reinstalled Windows. But I'm glad I did... there was soooo much crap in my registry for stuff that I had uninstalled months ago, even for hardware that is no longer in my computer.  Norton System Works wouldn't even let me delete the crap.  The registry sucks... what a dumb idea.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
